# /srv/gufo-qwen38-27b/.env — runtime layout for the Gufo Qwen3.8-27B engine,
# managed by kwisatz tasks/setup-gufo-strix-halo-qwen38-27b.sh
# (mode 600, owned by the installing user).
#
# This file is the ONLY place a stack setting lives. Both wrappers source it,
# so a change here is picked up on the next load — no re-run, no re-render.
#
# A re-run rewrites the keys this script owns (PORT, CONTAINER_NAME, paths,
# engine ref) and carries over every other KEY= line you added, verbatim. So
# adding a lever is safe; editing one of ours is not (it will be re-rendered
# from the task's defaults).
#
# Gufo's own flags are NOT here: run
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint gufo ${GUFO_IMAGE} serve llm --help
# and put what you need into GUFO_EXTRA_ARGS below. That is the escape hatch
# and it needs no file edit, which is the point: a hand-edited wrapper is a
# wrapper that is not in the repo.
#
# Secret rule: nothing secret is ever substituted into a generated file. If a
# model ever needs a token, put HF_TOKEN=<token> in this file (mode 600) and
# the wrapper will pass it through when present.
#
# Quoting rule, so a re-run cannot undo it: values are double-quoted because
# this file is *sourced*, and `KEY=a b` sourced is `KEY=a` followed by running
# `b`. Empty values stay quoted for the same reason.

# ── Identity / lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host port Gufo listens on (loopback). llama-swap's llamaSwap.proxy points at
# exactly this; changing it here without re-running the task will NOT update
# the llama-swap entry — re-run ./setup-gufo-strix-halo-qwen38-27b.sh.
PORT=${PORT}
# Container name llama-swap's cmdStop stops. Must match models-entry.yml.
CONTAINER_NAME="${CONTAINER_NAME}"
# Where the prepared marker and logs live (must be writable by the llama-swap
# service, so under /srv — not under a home directory).
STATE_DIR="${STATE_DIR}"
# Hugging Face cache holding the checkpoint. This is the user's cache: the
# container bind-mounts it read-only and llama-swap never writes to it.
HF_CACHE="${HF_CACHE}"
# Catalog id the container reports in responses (--served-model-name). Keep it
# equal to the models.yml entry id, or clients that echo model back will look
# like they are talking to a different model.
GUFO_MODEL_NAME="${GUFO_MODEL_NAME}"
# Engine image. Set it here to try a different build without a re-install.
GUFO_IMAGE="${GUFO_IMAGE}"

# ── ROCm / iGPU ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# gfx1151 is not in ROCm's autodetect table, so the override is mandatory —
# 11.5.1 is what the Strix Halo runs use. Dropping it makes the engine fall
# back to a generic target and fail on the first allocation.
HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=${HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION}
# Strix Halo has no discrete SDMA engines; leaving SDMA on selects paths that
# do not exist on this silicon.
HSA_ENABLE_SDMA=${HSA_ENABLE_SDMA}
# Shared-memory size for the container. The engine's staging buffers live in
# /dev/shm; too small and a long prompt is truncated on a host error rather
# than a clean engine error.
GUFO_SHM_SIZE=${GUFO_SHM_SIZE}

# ── Concurrency / cache levers ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Parallel sessions. Each session carries its own KV state; this is the knob
# that trades first-token latency for throughput on a unified-memory part.
GUFO_SESSIONS=${GUFO_SESSIONS}
# Prompt-cache disk staging, in bytes. 0 = disabled (the default): caching
# 262 K-context prompts to disk costs ~8 GiB resident, which is real memory
# this machine would rather give the model. Turn it on only when the same long
# prompt is replayed over and over.
GUFO_CACHE_DISK_STAGING_BYTES=${GUFO_CACHE_DISK_STAGING_BYTES}

# ── Escape hatches (no file edit needed) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Passed verbatim to `gufo serve llm`.
GUFO_EXTRA_ARGS="${GUFO_EXTRA_ARGS}"

# ── Draft model / speculation ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DFlash2 lives in its own repo, so it gets its own read-only mount at /draft
# rather than being copied under /models. gufo-serve.sh resolves the snapshot
# and passes the path to the engine itself, with the flag the backend needs:
# `--speculative dflash2` plus `--dflash-model /draft/<file>`.
GUFO_DRAFT_REPO="${GUFO_DRAFT_REPO}"
GUFO_DRAFT_PATTERN="${GUFO_DRAFT_PATTERN}"
# On by default here, because this is the configuration the throughput numbers
# for this model were measured with. Empty it and the model still serves — at
# roughly half the rate, but correctly — which is why the wrapper appends the
# draft path itself rather than trusting a hand-written pair of flags.
# A newer Gufo is the one thing that can rename this flag:
#   docker run --rm --entrypoint gufo ${GUFO_IMAGE} serve llm --help
# Note that a value you clear here comes back on the next re-run, because this
# key belongs to the re-rendered set: run the task once with GUFO_SPEC_ARGS=
# in the environment to turn speculation off for good.
GUFO_SPEC_ARGS="${GUFO_SPEC_ARGS}"

# Fraction of the GPU aperture the engine may claim. Blank = the engine's own
# default. This model is 16.4 GiB of weights, so the number matters most when
# the Flash-Next stack is installed next to it.
GUFO_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=${GUFO_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION}
# Passed verbatim to `docker run` (extra mounts, ulimits, --gpus-style flags).
CONTAINER_EXTRA_ARGS="${CONTAINER_EXTRA_ARGS}"
